# Expected skips on the ubuntu-latest lane (plain xfrm build; not configured
# with --enable-keymat-oracle, so run.sh's addke_ok is false even though ADDKE
# itself auto-builds on this runner's OpenSSL 3.5).  With
# R2_REQUIRE_LIVE=1 any other skip fails the run.
#   row <name> <why>   |   gate <gate> <why>
gate addke PQC rows need the keymat-oracle: addke_ok requires WITH_ADDKE AND
  WITH_KEYMAT_ORACLE, and the plain xfrm build lacks the oracle -> Fedora's
  xfrm-addke lane (--enable-addke --enable-keymat-oracle) runs i2ike-reqdrop
gate charonv1 strongSwan >= 6.1 (resident on some 24.04/sid peers) has no IKEv1; skipped only when libcharon proves it (run.sh charon_ikev1_absent)
gate dpd   11-timer DPD ladder (~16 min) is box-only
gate box   new rows are box-verified before CI admits them
gate pfkey  Linux pfkey-backend rows run in the pfkey lane only
gate nsim  netdevsim ESP offload absent from this kernel build; skipped only on the printed refusal (run.sh nsim_offload_probe)
gate xfrmmig Libreswan refuses mobike=yes without CONFIG_XFRM_MIGRATE; lwpeer-mobike-{i,r} skipped only on the kernel's ENOPROTOOPT (run.sh xfrm_migrate_absent)
